---
/** A cutting of the toile de Jouy for the sample-book swatch: engraved garden
    scenes in one ink (oxblood by day, gold on hunter in the lacquered room),
    after Huet. The drawing is an external SVG per scheme (assets/toile-*.svg,
    built by scripts/themes/proofs/stage5-gm-toile + scripts/themes/grandmillennial/build-patterns.mjs)
    that the browser caches; this is only the frame it is cut in.

    A swatch is not one size (353 x 441 at 1440, 258 x 322 at 820, 353 x 199 on
    a phone), and a background is anchored to its top left, so one fixed offset
    would cut the scenes at the edges. The cutting is a square 1000px field
    centred on the swatch (the swatch clips it), so the scenes sit the same way
    at every size: one cut of the cloth for the portrait swatch, a second,
    wider one under 720px. The offsets come from
    scripts/themes/proofs/stage5-gm-toile/find-swatch-frames.mjs. */
interface Props { class?: string }
const { class: cls } = Astro.props;
---
<div class:list={['gm-toile', cls]} aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
  .gm-toile {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%; top: 50%;
    width: 1000px; height: 1000px;
    margin: -500px 0 0 -500px;
    background: url('../assets/toile-light.svg') 481px 98px / 507px 576px repeat;
  }
  :global(html[data-scheme='dark']) .gm-toile { background-image: url('../assets/toile-dark.svg'); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .gm-toile { background-position: 125px 440px; background-size: 465px 528px; }
  }
</style>
